 "method": "Same pipeline as the v1 (XC1093538) measurement: STFT (1024-pt Hann, 128 hop) dominant-peak pitch track in 1.3-9.5 kHz; note segmentation on the 1.5-9 kHz band Hilbert envelope (3 ms smoothing): body pass onset -24 dB / offset -31 dB rel. file peak, min off-time 15 ms, min note 25 ms; sensitive pass onset -32 / offset -38 dB, extras kept only if non-overlapping with body notes and spectral-peak prominence >= 10 dB. Note f_start/f_end = median track over first/last 20% of the note; f_peak/f_min = 95th/5th percentile. peak_amp_rel = max of the 1.5-9 kHz band envelope (linear, signal peak-normalized) within the note. Contour and amplitude templates = per-note tracks resampled to 16 normalized points, median across instances of the type. Bouts = note groups split at gaps > 1.0 s. Type rules (this bird, by contour): U (upslur) = f_end - f_start >= 600 Hz, split by duration: Ua = dur < 0.44 s, Ub = dur >= 0.44 s; C (high chip) = f_start >= 3400 Hz, f_end <= 2700 Hz and f_start - f_end >= 1700 Hz (steep plunge; two of the 17 land near 2.5 kHz instead of 1.65 kHz \u2014 same gesture, shallower landing); D (downslur) = f_start <= 2600 Hz, f_end <= 1750 Hz, f_peak <= 2600 Hz. Contamination scan (new in v2): short-time RMS in 0.25 s windows for the 60-500 Hz band and full band; a swell = 1 s-smoothed level > file median + 7 dB sustained >= 1.5 s (spans < 2 s apart merged).",
